{# What people are saying, beside a grid of drawings: Home's feeds, each
   with the comments of its own people or places (handlers/home.rs,
   Feed::comment_scope), and a community's drawings with the start of its
   comments page, which `all_url` links to.

   One markup for every width; style.css decides where it goes. On a wide
   window it is a column beside the grid that stays in view as the grid
   scrolls, and scrolls on its own when it is longer than the window. Below
   that it is a row of cards between the feed's header and its grid, swiped
   across rather than scrolled past, so a phone reaches the drawings at
   once. The feed's section lays it out (`.feed-layout`), so it comes after
   the header and before the grid, which is the order it reads in at every
   width.

   Nothing to show, nothing rendered, and the grid has the width to itself. #}
{% import "comment_card_macro.jinja" as comment_card_macro %}
{% macro comments_aside(comments, all_url=none) %}
  {% if comments %}
    <aside class="feed-comments" aria-labelledby="feed-comments-title">
      <div class="feed-comments-head">
        <h2 id="feed-comments-title" class="feed-comments-title">{{ ftl_get_message("recent-comments") }}</h2>
        {% if all_url %}
          <a class="feed-comments-all" href="{{ all_url }}">{{ ftl_get_message("recent-comments-all") }}</a>
        {% endif %}
      </div>
      <div class="feed-comments-list">
        {% for comment in comments %}
          {{ comment_card_macro.comment_card(comment, r2_public_endpoint_url, ftl_get_message) }}
        {% endfor %}
      </div>
    </aside>
  {% endif %}
{% endmacro %}
